Subject: Tweak: mirror match
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509

In Domination's captain select, a captain one team has picked is greyed out
and the other team cannot pick him: OnCaptainPointerEnter and
OnCaptainPointerPress refuse him, and RefreshCaptainImages shows his
disabled portrait. The title screen's demo matches avoid the same captain
too. With "Mirror match" enabled, offline Domination keeps that captain lit
and available, so both teams can have the same captain. The Road to the
Striker Cup and online or LAN matches keep the original rule.

CharacterLoader has a branch for one captain on both teams, which the
retail game never reaches: it dresses the away team's captain and sidekicks
in the captain's away kit. The tweak completes it:

- The away goalie wears the away kit as well.
- Mario, Luigi, Wario and Waluigi have no away kit on the disc; the branch
  would have asked for textures that do not exist. Their away kit is made as
  the home kit loads (the port's src/platform/away_kits.cpp): the kit
  texture of the captain's model and the team textures of his goalie and
  sidekicks are recoloured into blue for Mario, sky blue for Luigi, blue for
  Wario and orange for Waluigi, and registered under the away kit's name.
  Sidekick and goalie team textures are compared with the same texture of
  two other teams, read from the disc, so only their team colour changes.
- The away team wears its kit and colour in the menus and the match's
  overlays too. NeedsAlternateColour and GetTeamColour cannot tell two teams
  of one captain apart, so these hooks pass the side: the player indicators
  and the defensive play overlay on the field; captain and sidekick select,
  Choose Sides and the pointers in the menus; the holograms, the HUD's
  captain icon, the goal banner's emblem, the super ability picture, the
  Mega Strike hand and the newspaper photo of an away winner. Where the game
  has a whole away kit, the one a captain wears against a captain of his
  colours (Bowser, Bowser Jr., Daisy, Diddy Kong, Donkey Kong, Petey and
  Yoshi), its own pictures show; the icon, banner, super ability picture and
  photo stay as the game has them. For the others the home pictures are
  recoloured: the portrait in the away PDA and the captain on the sidekick
  field plan (copies added to the front end's pool with the scene,
  MirrorMatchAwayPicture); the sidekick images, HUD icon, super ability
  picture and newspaper photo as each load completes (sidekick images
  compared with the same image of two other teams; photos only for Mario,
  as the others' have their colour in the background); the banner's emblem
  texture, switched in place between its home and away versions; the
  hologram's kit (its home textures load once more as the alternate ones)
  and the Mega Strike hand (the captain's extra textures load once more).
  Peach's blue field kit and hologram are on the disc; her pictures and hand
  are made.
- Choose Sides shows both teams' captain as holograms. An impostor's render
  targets are named after its character (ImpostorCharacter), so the away
  hologram would draw into the home one's targets, and destroying both
  would free them twice. A character already shown gets targets of its own.

A captain on both teams otherwise loads like a sidekick kind on both teams,
which the game allows: one template, and a sound bank slot per team.

